# PlanningWorkspace - Workflow Doctrine

`<workspace>` below refers to the Workspace path from `## Configuration` in the parent `CLAUDE.md`.

This folder holds shared, read-only clones of the repos referenced by the dev workflow. It is refreshed by `/status` (Phase 1).

**Rules:**
- READ ONLY — never modify files in this folder
- Never switch branches
- Never commit or push
- Always on the `main` branch

**Update command (run before planning):**
```bash
cd <workspace>/PlanningWorkspace
for dir in */; do (cd "$dir" && git fetch origin && git reset --hard origin/main); done
```

## Repo Registry

The repo registry lives in **`repos.md`** (this folder). It is user-owned — the plugin never overwrites it, and `/workspace-init refresh` leaves it untouched (this CLAUDE.md, by contrast, is plugin-managed and IS overwritten on refresh — don't add personal content here).

When work touches a repo not listed in `repos.md`, obtain its clone URL — from the ticket, the user, or an existing clone's `git remote get-url origin` — and append a row before proceeding. Keep its optional "Quick Reference: Which Repo?" section current the same way when planning reveals task→repo routing knowledge.

## NuGet Dependencies

Packages come from remote feeds only. No local package workflow.

If work requires NuGet package changes:
1. Document in Discussion
2. Wait for package publish
3. Update references and continue

**UI Stubbing:** If UI depends on pending package changes, create stubs marked with `// TODO: Remove stub when [PackageName] published`. Don't stub if it isn't necessary.

## Coding patterns

This template doesn't ship coding-pattern rules — teams and individual engineers manage those themselves. If you want path-scoped coding rules in this workspace, drop your own files into `<workspace>\.claude\rules\` (see https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory#path-specific-rules for the `paths:` frontmatter format).
